course: dictionary
lesson: 666
title: Baked: one word, two jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word baked can be a verb or an adjective, and the sentence shows you which. «She baked a cake» is the past form of bake: baked is the action that already happened, when she cooked the cake.
explain: When baked comes before a thing, like «baked potato» or «baked beans», it is an adjective. It describes the food and means cooked in an oven. Ask yourself: is this word showing an action, or describing a thing? That question solves most cases.
explain: Baked can also mean dried hard by heat. «Settled people made pots of baked clay» means the clay was heated until it went hard, not that it was eaten. To check, swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Bake is the verb, and baked is its past form, as in «She baked a cake».
fact: «Baked potato» and «baked beans» mean cooked in an oven.
fact: «Baked clay» and «baked mud» mean dried hard by heat.
fact: «Half-baked» means not well thought out, so it is not about cooking at all.
fact: Baked goods are foods like bread and cakes that have been cooked in an oven.
exercise: «Settled people made pots of baked clay to store grain.» What does baked mean here? | Cooked in an oven for dinner | *Dried hard by heat | Thrown away | Painted in bright colours
exercise: «He baked a cake for the school fair.» Is baked a verb or an adjective here? | Adjective, describing the cake | *Verb, the past form of bake | Noun, a name for a shop | Adverb, meaning very quickly
exercise: Ava says a «half-baked idea» is a cake that was not cooked enough. What does it really mean? | *Not well thought out | Cooked in an oven | Dried hard by the sun | Very tasty
test: «The Indus cities had houses of baked bricks, all the same size.» What does baked mean here? | Broken into small pieces | *Dried hard by heat to make a brick | Cooked in an oven for dinner | Painted in bright colours
test: Max eats «baked beans» on toast. What does baked mean in this phrase? | Not well thought out | Dried hard by the sun | Made of clay | *Cooked in an oven
exam: «A pencil is a rod of graphite mixed with clay, baked, then glued and painted.» What does baked mean in this sentence? | *Heated until hard | Cooked as a meal | Painted in bright colours | Sharpened to a point
